# Fabricated fixture credentials. Every environment in this repo invents its own data, and an
# API key is one of the things a fixture has to invent: parserail's key format is fixed at
# `ksk_live_` + 40 hex by KEY_PREFIX in the product's lib/platform/keys.ts, and the auth path
# rejects anything else, so a fixture key that did not look like a live key would be testing a
# format the product does not have.
#
# The key below is `ksk_live_11aa22bb33cc44dd55ee66ff77008811992200aa`, which is a hand-typed
# repeating pattern rather than 40 random hex, and the second finding is its SHA-256, which is
# what the product actually stores. Checked against production 2026-09-19: zero rows in the live
# key table carry that hash, so no real credential exists with this value and there is nothing to
# rotate.
